MCP setup for Generic MCP JSON
Add to: your MCP client's mcpServers configuration

{
  "mcpServers": {
    "eshu": {
      "headers": {
        "Authorization": "Bearer ${ESHU_MCP_TOKEN}"
      },
      "type": "http",
      "url": "http://127.0.0.1:18091/mcp/message"
    }
  }
}

Create a personal API token in the Eshu console: https://<host>/profile
(Profile -> API tokens), then export it before launching the client:
  export ESHU_MCP_TOKEN=...
The token authenticates you as yourself; it is scoped to your grants.

Notes:
  - Most MCP clients accept this "mcpServers" object; place it where your client expects.
